<div class="container safety-page">
    <section class="safety-hero">
        <div class="safety-hero-copy">
            <span class="safety-eyebrow">SDUT SWAP · SMART TRADING GUIDE</span>
            <h1>Stay sharp.<br><span>Swap safely.</span></h1>
            <p>A good deal should feel good from the first message to the final handover. Use these practical tips to protect yourself when buying and selling on campus.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/listings">Browse listings <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="safety-hero-art" aria-hidden="true"><div class="safety-shield">✓</div><span class="safety-spark safety-spark-one">✦</span><span class="safety-spark safety-spark-two">✧</span></div>
    </section>

    <div class="safety-alert"><span aria-hidden="true">!</span><p><strong>Remember:</strong> SDUT Swap helps students connect, but it cannot guarantee a transaction or verify the condition of an item. You are responsible for making careful decisions before paying or handing anything over.</p></div>

    <section class="safety-section">
        <div class="safety-section-heading"><span class="safety-kicker">BEFORE YOU MEET</span><h2>Prepare before making a deal</h2><p>A little preparation can prevent most avoidable problems.</p></div>
        <div class="safety-tip-grid">
            <article class="safety-tip-card"><span class="safety-tip-number">01</span><div class="safety-tip-icon">🔎</div><h3>Check the listing carefully</h3><p>Read the full description, compare the photos, and check the stated condition, price, and included accessories. Ask about scratches, defects, missing parts, or repairs.</p></article>
            <article class="safety-tip-card"><span class="safety-tip-number">02</span><div class="safety-tip-icon">💬</div><h3>Ask clear questions</h3><p>Confirm the exact item, final price, meeting place, and time in chat. For electronics, ask about battery health, functionality, ownership, and whether the device is locked.</p></article>
            <article class="safety-tip-card"><span class="safety-tip-number">03</span><div class="safety-tip-icon">💸</div><h3>Be realistic about the price</h3><p>Compare similar listings. An unusually low price, pressure to pay immediately, or a story designed to rush you should make you pause and investigate.</p></article>
            <article class="safety-tip-card"><span class="safety-tip-number">04</span><div class="safety-tip-icon">🧑‍🤝‍🧑</div><h3>Tell someone your plan</h3><p>Let a friend know where and when you are meeting. For expensive items or if you feel uncertain, ask someone you trust to accompany you.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section">
        <div class="safety-section-heading"><span class="safety-kicker">DURING THE EXCHANGE</span><h2>Meet smart. Inspect first. Pay last.</h2><p>Keep the handover simple, public, and unhurried.</p></div>
        <div class="safety-checklist">
            <article><span>📍</span><div><h3>Choose a public campus location</h3><p>Meet during busy daytime hours in a familiar, well-lit place such as a student center, library entrance, or another public campus area. Avoid isolated rooms, private homes, and unfamiliar locations.</p></div></article>
            <article><span>🕒</span><div><h3>Don't let anyone rush you</h3><p>If the other person changes the location at the last minute, pressures you to hurry, or makes you uncomfortable, pause or cancel. You do not owe anyone a transaction.</p></div></article>
            <article><span>🧪</span><div><h3>Inspect and test the item</h3><p>Check that it matches the listing. Test electronics, buttons, ports, screens, and accessories where possible. For books, check the edition and missing pages; for clothing, check size and condition.</p></div></article>
            <article><span>💳</span><div><h3>Pay only after inspection</h3><p>Do not send deposits or full payment just to reserve an item unless you have independently verified the arrangement and are comfortable with the risk. Confirm the amount and recipient before authorizing a transfer.</p></div></article>
            <article><span>🧾</span><div><h3>Keep a transaction record</h3><p>Keep relevant chat details and payment confirmations. If you agree on a different price or item condition, make sure both sides clearly confirm it in writing before completing the exchange.</p></div></article>
            <article><span>🤝</span><div><h3>Be respectful and fair</h3><p>Be on time, describe items honestly, and respect the other person's decision to walk away. Never threaten, harass, or pressure someone into buying or selling.</p></div></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section safety-two-column">
        <div>
            <span class="safety-kicker">PROTECT YOUR ACCOUNT</span>
            <h2>Keep your personal information private</h2>
            <p>Your privacy matters just as much as the item you are trading. Share only what is necessary to arrange a safe campus exchange.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="safety-privacy-list">
            <p><strong>Never share passwords or verification codes.</strong> No buyer, seller, or support representative needs your password or one-time login code.</p>
            <p><strong>Keep private details private.</strong> Avoid posting your home address, room number, student ID, passport, bank card, or other identity documents in listings or chat.</p>
            <p><strong>Be cautious with links and files.</strong> Do not open suspicious payment links, QR codes, attachments, or websites sent by strangers.</p>
            <p><strong>Use platform conversations.</strong> Keeping deal details in SDUT Swap gives you a clearer record if you need to report a problem.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-scam-panel">
        <div class="safety-scam-heading"><span class="safety-kicker">RED FLAGS</span><h2>Recognize common scam patterns</h2><p>Stop and reassess if you notice any of these warning signs.</p></div>
        <div class="safety-redflag-grid">
            <div><b>01</b><span><strong>Advance-payment pressure</strong><small>They demand a deposit before you can see or inspect the item.</small></span></div>
            <div><b>02</b><span><strong>Fake payment proof</strong><small>A screenshot or message claims payment was sent, but the money is not in your account.</small></span></div>
            <div><b>03</b><span><strong>Overpayment stories</strong><small>They send too much money and ask you to refund the difference.</small></span></div>
            <div><b>04</b><span><strong>Suspicious links</strong><small>They ask you to log in or enter bank details on an unfamiliar website.</small></span></div>
            <div><b>05</b><span><strong>Moving off-platform</strong><small>They insist on switching apps immediately and refuse to keep basic details in platform chat.</small></span></div>
            <div><b>06</b><span><strong>Unusual delivery arrangements</strong><small>They introduce an unknown courier, extra fees, or complicated payment steps.</small></span></div>
            <div><b>07</b><span><strong>Identity or account requests</strong><small>They ask for passwords, verification codes, student credentials, or remote access to your device.</small></span></div>
            <div><b>08</b><span><strong>Too-good-to-be-true offers</strong><small>The price or story seems designed to stop you asking normal questions.</small></span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-section">
        <div class="safety-section-heading"><span class="safety-kicker">SELLER CHECKLIST</span><h2>Selling safely on campus</h2><p>Protect your item, your time, and your information.</p></div>
        <div class="safety-seller-grid">
            <article><h3>Write an honest description</h3><p>Use clear photos you took yourself. Mention defects, wear, repairs, and exactly what is included. Do not hide problems to get a higher price.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Remove personal data</h3><p>Before selling a phone, laptop, or tablet, back up your files, sign out of accounts, remove personal information, and reset the device securely.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Confirm payment yourself</h3><p>Check your own banking or payment app. Never rely only on an email, text, screenshot, or a buyer's phone as proof of payment.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Hand over only when ready</h3><p>Do not give the item away because someone shows a pending transfer. Complete the handover only when you have confirmed the agreed payment.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-report">
        <div class="safety-report-icon">🛡</div>
        <div><span class="safety-kicker">SOMETHING DOESN'T FEEL RIGHT?</span><h2>Stop the deal and report it.</h2><p>If you see a suspicious listing, receive threatening messages, or experience a problem, stop communicating if necessary and use the platform's reporting tools. Keep relevant screenshots and transaction records. For immediate danger or suspected crime, contact campus security or local authorities.</p><a href="/support">Visit Support Center <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="safety-final-note"><strong>The golden rule</strong><p>If something feels wrong, walk away. No bargain is worth risking your safety, money, or personal information.</p></section>
</div>
